// * THE HOUSE GRID (CHARTS_RESTYLE.md section 3). Kyser: "the charts all over the terminal are
// super duper ugly". The saturation he sees is the WIDTH, the ALPHA and the vertical grid, not the
// hues -- so the style lands in ONE place, baseLayout(), which about 95% of the terminal's draw
// sites already call. Three normalisations, all deliberate:
//   - the y grid is always the house line #ebe6d8, so the terminal has exactly ONE grid colour;
//   - a few call sites asked for NO grid by painting it a colour the eye cannot see (transparent,
//     or the paper itself). That intent is kept by turning showgrid OFF -- the grid still does not
//     draw; only the dormant token changes;
